{{$NEXT}}
  - Introduce the SimpiCI distribution with normalized events, exact detached
    checkouts, filesystem state and public JSON/log reports. Local logs are
    unredacted; worker uploads redact assigned secret values.
  - Poll GitHub and Forgejo mirrors with independent observations, including
    newly appearing refs after initial polling. Shared durable run
    deduplication is provided by the dispatcher queue. A repository whose refs
    cannot be read (git ls-remote fails), or that returns none of the
    configured refs while tips are recorded for it, does not stop simpicid: it
    logs one "not polled" line naming the repository, its clone URL and the
    reason, polls the remaining repositories, keeps
    the recorded tips and tries again in the next cycle, so refs that return
    are not built as new. simpicid --once polls every repository and exits
    with 1 if one was not polled. SimpiCI::Source::GitPoll offers observe and
    rejection; poll accepts an observation.
  - simpicid gives up on a repository whose refs are not read within
    ls_remote_timeout seconds (new top-level setting, default 60), logs it as
    not polled and goes on with the next one. git ls-remote runs in its own
    process group that is ended together with its helpers, and it does not
    answer prompts on the terminal. A remote that prints a lot on standard
    error does not block the poller.
  - simpicid checks the clone URL of every configured repository when it
    starts, in local and in dispatcher mode, and exits before it polls if one
    carries credentials (http:// or https:// with a user part) or whitespace
    or control characters. The message names the repository and its position
    in the configuration, never the URL; credentials belong in a Git
    credential helper of the account that runs git. The rule is
    SimpiCI::Event->clone_url_rejection.
  - Dispatch durable leased jobs to outbound SSH workers, with fenced recovery
    and idempotent completion upload through a restricted worker protocol.
  - Scope dispatcher secret files to repositories, refs, events and publish or
    deploy phases; redact uploaded logs and keep values out of command lines.
    A grant ref is exact or a refs/<path>/* pattern (refs/tags/* covers every
    release tag); any other use of "*" is rejected as a configuration error.
    Every grant is checked when simpicid starts in dispatcher mode and before
    each claim: an unusable one (name, ref pattern, phases, secret file) is
    reported with its repository and secret, simpicid does not start, and no
    lease is taken, while completions are still accepted. A secret name may
    not be any variable the executor assigns itself (CICD_BRANCH, CICD_TAG,
    CICD_REGISTRY, CICD_REGISTRY_USER, ...); only CICD_REGISTRY_PASSWORD
    passes through. In dispatcher mode simpicid needs read access to the
    granted secret files.
  - Discover repository jobs from their filenames, execute them in selected
    containers and enforce ordered phase barriers with bounded same-phase
    concurrency (default 2).
  - Expose the artifacts of earlier phases to later jobs: every job gets
    CICD_INPUTS=/inputs with <phase>/<job>/ of each earlier phase mounted
    read-only. Jobs of the same phase never see each other, a job that wrote
    nothing leaves an empty directory, and nothing is transferred between
    workers or to the dispatcher.
  - Merge repository jobs and provider-generated jobs in a writable staging
    directory: operator-selected provider images (SIMPICI_PROVIDERS, exposed as
    the reusable workflow's "provider" input) generate additional .cicd/*.sh
    files, and the repository's own same-named jobs always win. Providers run
    read-only over the checkout with no registry credentials or Docker socket,
    letting a repository ship no .cicd at all.
  - Provide a reusable GitHub/Forgejo action and GitHub workflow for the same
    zero-configuration repository-job contract used by the native daemon.
  - Add complete POD manuals and conventional help output for both command-line
    programs, including explicit executor-path configuration.
  - Put reusable core classes under SimpiCI::* and command implementations
    under SimpiCI::App::*.
  - Install the shared phase executor as simpici-executor so CPAN, containers,
    GitHub and Forgejo use the same runnable implementation.
  - Expand the README, cookbook and operations reference with executable
    examples, distinguish current behavior from the planned branch policy,
    and remove obsolete planning notes.
  - Consolidate project agent instructions and skills under CLAUDE.md and
    .claude with no duplicate agent configuration.
  - Publish the daemon image primarily as raudssus/simpici on Docker Hub and
    mirror it to GHCR with independent CI jobs.
  - Run the dispatcher as a container (deploy/dispatcher): an image without
    Docker CLI, a Compose file with the poller and a restricted sshd endpoint
    (port 2222) for worker forced commands, plus example dispatcher
    configuration and authorized_keys. A .dockerignore keeps its state,
    secrets, SSH material and configuration out of every build context.
    Documented as section 5 of deploy/README.md.
